<article class="env-lemma" id="00WW">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00WW">Lemma <span data-tag="00WW">7.13.2</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ and $\mathcal{D}$ be sites. Let $u : \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{D}$ be a continuous functor. If $\mathcal{F}$ is a sheaf on $\mathcal{D}$ then $u^ p\mathcal{F}$ is a sheaf as well. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\{ V_ i \to V\} $ be a covering. By assumption $\{ u(V_ i) \to u(V)\} $ is a covering in $\mathcal{D}$ and $u(V_ i \times _ V V_ j) = u(V_ i)\times _{u(V)}u(V_ j)$. Hence the sheaf condition for $u^ p\mathcal{F}$ and the covering $\{ V_ i \to V\} $ is precisely the same as the sheaf condition for $\mathcal{F}$ and the covering $\{ u(V_ i) \to u(V)\} $. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>